NAME
       netd - network service supervisor

SYNOPSIS
       **netd**

DESCRIPTION
       Started by the kernel at boot. For every network interface except
       **lo** it turns off the kernel DHCP client and starts its own
       dhcpc(8), then restarts it when it exits (the delay grows from 2 to
       60 seconds). New interfaces, for example Wi-Fi after it connects, are
       picked up within two seconds.

       If /bin/netd is missing or fails to start, the kernel DHCP client keeps
       working as before.

SIGNALS
       **SIGTERM** stops all children, which release their leases.

SEE ALSO
       dhcpc(8), ip(8), services(5)
